 "learning_signals": [
  "Let's Encrypt helpers repeatedly point people at the staging environment and at --dry-run before touching production limits.",
  "Most HTTP-01 failures are reachability problems that are visible from outside only: people learn to test from an outside vantage point (a phone on mobile data, a cloud VM) rather than from the server itself.",
  "WireGuard is silent by design, so practitioners learn to read 'latest handshake' and tcpdump on UDP 51820 instead of expecting error messages.",
  "Mesh VPN users learn NAT types through 'relayed vs direct' (tailscale netcheck, netbird status -d).",
  "OPNsense forum threads show that DNS (split horizon, rebind protection, DNSSEC) is behind many problems that look like NAT or firewall bugs.",
  "Docker + UFW surprises are learned the hard way, often after an exposed database; seniors bind admin ports to 127.0.0.1 and use DOCKER-USER.",
  "Expiration emails ending in 2025 pushed people to build their own expiry monitoring (blackbox exporter, Uptime Kuma, small scripts)."
 ],
